extends layout.pug

block title
    title Tomokagízo

block body
    .head
        img(src="/static/atinu.png", alt="Atinú logo", width="100px")
        h1 Tomokagízo no Atinú
        p buoñorok a di tomokagízo no Atinú!<br>(welcome to the Atinú homepage!)
    .main 
        h2 about
        p
        | welcome to the project that took me 5yrs to complete (i started in 2020)<br>
        | Atinú is a conlang, more specifically an auxlang which was designed to be easy to learn and use in literature, poetry, music, etc<br>
        | it has its own pseudo-history, culture, writing system, and philosophy... kinda like any natural language<br>
        | main roots of it are PIE, proto-germanic, latin, japanese, and various other languages :P

        h2 pseudo-history
        p
        | it originates from a small nomadic tribe called the Atinitose (literally: Atinú humans) that lived near modern-day germany, switzerland, and italy<br>
        | they were mainly poets that traveled around the world to perform for food and other necessities<br>
        | eventually, they travel to asia, and incorporate many of the languaes and philosophies they encounter into their own language<br>
        br
        | people who usually left the nomadic life and settled down developed a slight accent (settler's accent) which had the sounds /t d f v/ unlike the nomads
        | who used /t̪ d̪ ɸ β/ instead<br>
        | so if you want to sound more sophisticated, use the nomadic accent, otherwise the settler's accent is fine<br>
        | thats about it :P

        h2 philosophy
        p
        | the main thing about Atinú is that it only has 190 or so <i>roots</i><br>
        | however, the gender/noun-class system has 3 forms, xert (heart/abstract/root), oso (animate/alive), and śuk (inanimate/dead)<br>
        | changing the gender of a root along with context can change the meaning drastically, for example:<br>
        | sakan: to fish, to be like fish, peaceful, wise<br>
        | sakano: fish, marine life<br>
        | sakanuk: dead fish, foolish being (insult)<br>
        br
        | this is supposed show the cycle between life and death, and how it is a constant cycle, spinning like a wheel :P<br>
        | yes i know... very yin-yang... dont make fun of me -w- hehehe
        br
        | one more thing is that no word has a concrete meaning? you just know what it vaguely represents, and the way you structure the sentence<br>
        | and the context of the conversation will be deciding factor for the actual meaning of the words<br>
        | sort of the fluidity that could help with poetry, and also similar to the philosophy of "goin with the flow" lol

        h2 use
        p
        | this project is licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank">CC BY-SA 4.0</a><br>
        | feel free to use it however you like, as long as you give proper credit to me (owlly) and share it under the same license<br>
        | thank you :3
